From c2266bb4115322d528b69dcc330ac77263a606dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tatsuki Tanaka <tatsuki@tanakatatsuki.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:40:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: support topology-driven legacy TDM
 modules

Keep the legacy TDM endpoints for the SM8475 ADSP and configure them from the same framing and lane tokens as Audio IF.

Source changes (original messages and trailers follow).

Source-commit: f56af7557d15cfb10cef112c0b3c41da986c52b6
Source-author: Tatsuki Tanaka <tatsuki@tanakatatsuki.dev>
Source-date: 2026-10-09T18:40:28+08:00
Link: https://github.com/iLtanaka/linux-marble/commit/3a2d02f13d1e22a50a12902aa273ad3aaf76457c
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/linux-marble/0052-ASoC-qcom-audioreach-add-TDM-DAI-ops-and-modules.patch

ASoC: qcom: audioreach: add TDM DAI ops and modules

Add TDM sink and source graph modules, tertiary TDM bit clock support,
and AudioReach DAI operations for multi-channel TDM routing on SM8450.

Signed-off-by: Tatsuki Tanaka <tatsuki@tanakatatsuki.dev>

(cherry picked from commit 3a2d02f13d1e22a50a12902aa273ad3aaf76457c)

Conflict resolution for Linux 7.3: 7.3 already has TDM DAI operations
(4d0840175893: q6tdm_ops with set_tdm_slot) and stores the slot layout
in audioreach_module_config.{slot_mask,nslots_per_frame,slot_width}
(67605cbf8dfe); the q6apm-lpass-dais.c hunk is dropped and the TDM
media format reads those fields instead of the tdm_* ones. The TDM
sink/source modules, PARAM_ID_TDM_INTF_CFG/LANE_CFG, their topology
loader case and the tertiary TDM clocks are kept as in the original.

Source-commit: 9128f6e75db4c74893fe2b92d5a04121aece69ad
Source-author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Source-date: 2026-10-25T09:48:44+08:00
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/local/0053-ASoC-qcom-audioreach-take-legacy-TDM-framing-from-th.patch

ASoC: qcom: audioreach: take legacy TDM framing from the topology

The TDM sink/source modules (0x0700100E/0x0700100F) took their frame
sync source, framing and data output enable from the DAI format set by
the machine driver. In Linux 7.3 the sc8280xp TDM path only sets the
clock provider (SND_SOC_DAIFMT_BP_FP), and the topology-driven Audio IF
modules (67605cbf8dfe) describe the serial interface through topology
tokens instead.

Load the Audio IF tokens for the TDM modules as well (sync source, data
output enable, sync mode, sync inversion, data delay, slot layout and
active lanes) in addition to the I2S interface tokens, and build
PARAM_ID_TDM_INTF_CFG from them. Slot count, width and mask still come
from the DAI TDM slots first, then the topology, then the stream.

The SM8475 ADSP of the Xiaomi Poco F5 (ADSP.HT.5.7-01183) registers the
TDM, I2S and codec DMA endpoint modules but not MODULE_ID_AUDIO_IF_*
(no 0x0700117C/0x0700117D in its image), so these boards need the
legacy modules with a board topology.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
